<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Share Extension entitlements — deliberately the bare minimum.

  App Sandbox only. No network, no file access, no app group, no keychain sharing. The extension
  reads a string the system already handed it and opens a `volar://` URL; it touches nothing else,
  so it asks for nothing else. Every entitlement added here is one more thing App Review asks about
  and one more thing that can go wrong in provisioning.

  Same hand-written-file discipline as the app's own Resources/Volar.entitlements: project.yml
  points CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS straight at this path and never uses XcodeGen's `entitlements:`
  generator key, which would overwrite this file on every `xcodegen generate`. If a new entitlement
  is ever genuinely needed, edit this file by hand.

  NOTE: `com.apple.security.app-sandbox` is mandatory for an app extension — unlike the app itself,
  an extension cannot opt out.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
